Classes. Every fixture marked "upstream form" or "upstream shape" below is
reviewed-upstream: its rendering is traced to the official systemd source of
tags v255 and v259, read from the official systemd/systemd GitHub repository.
Every fixture marked SYNTHETIC is a synthetic negative input: a malformed or
version-variant rendering that v255/v259 do not print, authored for the tests
and labelled as such; it claims no upstream provenance beyond the rule it
violates. Both tags render every value below the same
way; the one code difference on these paths (v259 no longer clears
LastTriggerUSec on timer start, R10) does not change a never-fired timer. None was
executed, built or captured. Every fixture here was not captured from Hotel-Echo,
nor from any other host.

Claim, and its limit. These fixtures make NO claim about Hotel-Echo's actual
runtime output. They validate the diagnostic mechanism against the upstream
`systemctl show -p <Property> --value` rendering forms; they do not prove what
Hotel-Echo's systemd (259) prints for these units. Where a field's value is not
established by the source (marked "normalized"), the launcher never parses it.

